From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:44:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] unicode: implement default case conversion in
 Unicode-Lite

Replace the no-op Unicode-Lite casing hook with full Unicode default lower- and uppercase mappings. Generate compact mappings and expansions from the pinned Unicode 17 data independently of regular-expression case folding. Handle supplementary code points, preserve unpaired surrogates, and apply Final_Sigma context to the original input.

Keep output storage local to each conversion and retain a direct ASCII path. Unicode-Lite still has no locale database: explicit language-sensitive casing and normalization remain outside this change. Add platform and JavaScript regressions for expansions, case-ignorable context, Cyrillic, supplementary characters, and long strings.

Validation: ten native PlatformUnicode tests, byte-identical table regeneration, and optimized Wasm execution of the JavaScript regression against V8.
